<title>PHILIPPINES: MANILA'S PHIBOR RATES MIXED AS MARKET CONSOLIDATES.</title>
<headline>MANILA'S PHIBOR RATES MIXED AS MARKET CONSOLIDATES.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mixed on Tuesday as the market went into consolidation after last week's slide, traders said.</p>
<p>A foreign bank dealer said the market was waiting for the central bank to further cut its overnight rates after Treasury bill rates fell in the auction on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;With the peso getting weaker on Tuesday, it may take quite some time before the central bank drops its rate,&quot; the trader said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  AUG 12		 AUG 11</p>
<p>    1 W		18  1/4		 18 3/8</p>
<p>    2 W		17  3/4		 17 3/4</p>
<p>    1 M		17  5/16		17 3/8</p>
<p>    2 M		16  9/16		16 3/4</p>
<p>    3 M		16  5/16		16 7/16</p>
<p>    6 M		16  7/16		16 3/8</p>
<p>    12M		15 15/16		15 3/4</p>
<p>    VAL		13-Aug		  12-Aug</p>
